  "topIssues": [
    {
      "id": "I_kwDOL-xLQ88AAAABIOmHbg",
      "title": "proxyd: eth_call for out-of-range block returns \"result\":null instead of an error",
      "author": "bLd75",
      "number": 666,
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "body": "**Bug Description**\n\nSince v4.25.1, the fix for #546 (PR #552) synthesizes spec-compliant responses for out-of-range block requests instead of returning an error. The method switch in `OverwriteConsensusRequests` ([backend.go#L2008-L2031](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/infra/blob/da202abd7c1c1c722d5850468330c33fe869dd7f/proxyd/backend.go#L2008-L2031)) handles the block-fetch methods correctly, but `eth_call` isn't listed and falls into default. This returns `\"result\": null` as a successful response.\n\nFor `eth_call` this isn't spec-compliant: it must return call data or an error. \nSome ABI clients crash on null result, and don't retry or alert since it's a success response.\n\n**Steps to Reproduce**\n\n1. Run proxyd with a consensus-aware backend group.\n2. Request an eth_call at a block above the consensus head:\n\n```\nHEAD=$(curl -s $PROXYD -d '{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"eth_blockNumber\",\"params\":[]}' | jq -r .result)\ncurl -s $PROXYD -d \"{\\\"jsonrpc\\\":\\\"2.0\\\",\\\"id\\\":2,\\\"method\\\":\\\"eth_call\\\",\\\"params\\\":[{\\\"to\\\":\\\"0x...\\\",\\\"data\\\":\\\"0x...\\\"},\\\"$(printf '0x%x' $((HEAD+2)))\\\"]}\"\n```\nresponse: `{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"result\":null,\"id\":2}` - HTTP 200\n\n**Expected behavior**\n\nReturn an error, as in ≤ v4.24.0: `{\"error\":{\"code\":-32019,\"message\":\"block is out of range\"}}` (or the request forwarded to a backend, which would return block not found).\n\n**Environment Information:**\n\nofficial image `us-docker.pkg.dev/oplabs-tools-artifacts/images/proxyd:v4.27.1`\nPackage Version: v4.27.1 (introduced in v4.25.1, unchanged on main)\n\n**Configurations:**\n\n`routing_strategy = \"consensus_aware\"`\n2 backends in the group\nno backend/sender rate limiting\n\n**Additional context**\n\nAffected methods falling into `default:` today: `eth_call` and `eth_getProof`\n(both consensus-rewritten but absent from the response-synthesis switch).\n\nSuggested fix: `default:` should return `ErrBlockOutOfRange` (the ≤ v4.24.0 behavior), keeping null/empty synthesis limited to the explicitly whitelisted methods where that matches the spec.\n",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-09T14:32:17Z",
      "closedAt": null,
      "state": "OPEN",
      "commentCount": 0
    }
  ],
